#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Agent factory dispatcher: a file-based board that drives Scion agents
through work -> review -> security -> gate. Runs as the 'factory' user.
Stages run here first; a [hosts.<name>] helper takes the stages it lists only when this
host is full, as Pi jobs (bin/factory-remote). A ticket pinned to a host runs only there.

  factory add <project> "<title>" [--body TEXT | --body-file F] [--door human|clock|github|peer] [--triage]
                                  [--host auto|local|<name>] [--task | --intent | --manage] [--timeout MIN]
  factory add <project> --recipe NAME   file a standing recipe ([[recipes]], or any schedule) now
  factory recipes [--json]            the recipes: each [[recipes]] entry and every schedule, to run on demand
  factory result <ticket>             a task's answer, or an intent's design and proposed tickets
  factory approve <ticket> [--only 1,3]   file the design's tickets (ready); redirect <ticket> --note TEXT
  factory host <ticket> auto|local|<name>
  factory ls [--all]
  factory show <ticket>
  factory model       the board's model as JSON (columns, stages, asks); Foreman embeds it as foreman/model.json
  factory look <ticket> [--lines N]   the running agent's screen now (read-only)
  factory memory [<project> [<role>]] [--revert COMMIT]   what agents remembered (git log), or undo one change
  factory audit <ticket>   what happened and which gate decided (also logs/<ticket>/audit.md)
  factory proposals        open proposals from prospecting, in the blind panel's priority order
  factory pr <ticket>      push a ready_for_pr branch and open its PR (draft unless auto-merge eligible)
  factory ask <ticket> Q   a question about a ticket: one agent run reads the code (on its branch) and answers
  factory merge <ticket>   merge an auto-merge-eligible PR on your go-ahead (only the commit the gate checked)
  factory github           check the GitHub App installation (repos, permissions)
  factory gate-workflow <project>   print a GitHub Actions workflow that re-runs Gate 1 off the box (see below)
  factory move <ticket> <column> [--note TEXT]
  factory note <ticket> <text>   a note every later agent on the ticket follows
  factory reply <ticket> <text>  answer the agent's question (its stage carries on with the answer), else Ask
  factory wake        start a tick now instead of at the next timer (after a reply or an answer)
  factory migrate     one-off backfill for older boards: asks on waiting tickets, votes on proposals,
                      dropped proposals filed as rejected tickets; safe to run again
  factory tick        one scheduling pass (safe to run from a timer)
  factory sweep       file triage tickets for new open GitHub issues
  factory clock       file tickets for recurring checks that are due
  factory rebuild     rebuild this host's agent images (pinned versions, fresh OS packages); weekly timer
  factory versions    file a notice ticket when a pinned agent version has a newer release
  factory check       config problems: project modes, [board] people, tokens naming projects that are gone
  factory ticket VERB [--as NAME] [--wait S] --json   a ticket verb (create, get, list, mine, note, move, claim,
                      update, ask, answer, split, send, projects, whoami, reindex): JSON request on stdin, answer on stdout
  factory ticket get T0042 | list [--project P] | answer T0042 N TEXT   the same, for a person
  factory tokens add NAME --project P [--project P…] --can read,file,talk,work,plan | list [--json] | revoke NAME
"""
